|notes        = 
* ''Rebuttal's'' barrier will also instantly destroy missiles that are already within its radius when the ability is cast.
* The replicated missile will mimic all of the original missile's properties, which includes its range, width, speed, acceleration, angle (if a cone), height, and sight radius.
** Spell effects, as well as interactions with {{tip|spell shield}} and {{tip|projectile|projectile-interception}} effects, all vary based on the original missile that was replicated.
** The only exception to this is the copied missile's path, or trajectory, which is based on the [[targeting|targeting paradigm]] that the original missile used when fired by its source. The replicated missile acquires the original missile source as the target.
*** If the original missile was fired by a {{tip|unit-targeted|unit}} or {{tip|auto-targeted}} effect, the replicated missile will be fired as a homing missile with the target being the original missile source.
**** Healing projectiles, such as {{cai|Starcall|Soraka|Rejuvenation}} and {{cai|Aria of Perseverance|Sona}}, will instead target '''Mel'''.
*** If the original missile was fired via any other targeting paradigm, the replicated missile will by default fire in the direction of the original missile source at the time of replication. This includes {{tip|vector-targeted}} projectiles (currently only {{cai|Hextech Ray|Viktor}}), for which the origin will always be '''Mel's''' center (since she cannot control the cast point).
* The replicated missile will mimic all of the functions of and copy the behavior of the original missile, unless otherwise stated. This includes every aspect and effect of the missile conforming to the attack or spell from which the missile originated.
** The scaling of the effects of the copied missile is calculated using the original missile source's attributes (namely their [[champion statistic|stats]]). The damage of the missile only benefits from '''Mel's''' [[damage modifier]]s and [[magic penetration]], and not the original source's.
* The following missiles are destroyed, but not replicated:
** {{cai|Whirling Death|Draven}} on its way back to him.
** {{cai|Boomerang Throw|Gnar}} on its way back to him.
** {{cai|Test of Spirit|Illaoi}}
** {{cai|Boomerang Blade|Sivir}} on its way back to her.
** {{cai|Hijack|Sylas}}
** {{cai|Fear Beyond Death 2|Urgot|Mercy}} 
** {{cai|Bladecaller|Xayah}} and {{ai|Featherstorm|Xayah}}
** {{cai|Stretching Strikes|Zac}}
** Missiles fired from [[auto-targeted]] abilities that target each unit in an area and aren't targeting '''Mel'''.
*** Examples include {{cai|R|Brand}}, {{cai|R|Katarina}}, {{cai|R|Samira}}, and {{cai|E|Ryze}}.
* The following abilities will be stopped short of their trajectory without replication:
** {{cai|Emperor's Divide|Azir}}
** {{cai|Dark Sphere|Syndra|Spheres}} thrown with her {{ai|Scatter the Weak|Syndra}}
* '''Mel''' may occasionally fail to attribute {{iis|Echoes of Helia}} {{nies|Soul Siphon}} damage projectile to herself.{{bug}}
** This can cause the enemy to be able to kill their own allies, and gain all the kill's [[Kill#Rewards|rewards]].
* ''Rebuttal'' will play distinct sound cues from destroying and replicating projectiles fired from specific types of abilities:
** Non-ultimate ability missile: <span class="inline-audio" data-vol="0.25">[[File:Mel_Original_SFX_WReflect_Normal_buffactivate.ogg]]</span>
** Ultimate ability missile: <span class="inline-audio" data-vol="0.25">[[File:Mel_Original_SFX_WReflect_Ult_buffactivate.ogg]]</span>
** Ability with global or near-global range missile: <span class="inline-audio" data-vol="0.2">[[File:Mel_Original_SFX_WReflect_Global_buffactivate.ogg]]</span>
